        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "834782ba-199c-5c2f-87cc-89466a2b192d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Carolina, Puerto Rico; San Juan; Montrose; Colorado\n- Organizations: Luis Muñoz Marín International Airport; Montrose Regional Airport\n- People: Luis Muñoz Marín\n- Topics: airport identifiers; airport types\n\nFacts:\n- Luis Muñoz Marín International Airport is an international joint civil-military airport in suburban Carolina, Puerto Rico, 3 miles southeast of San Juan.\n- Luis Muñoz Marín International Airport uses the identifiers IATA SJU, ICAO TJSJ, and FAA LID SJU.\n- Luis Muñoz Marín International Airport is also called Aeropuerto Internacional Luis Muñoz Marín and Isla Verde International Airport.\n- Luis Muñoz Marín International Airport is named for Luis Muñoz Marín, Puerto Rico's first democratically elected governor.\n- Montrose Regional Airport is a non-towered public airport on the northwest side of Montrose in ZIP code 81401 in southwestern Colorado.\n- Montrose Regional Airport uses the identifiers IATA MTJ, ICAO KMTJ, and FAA LID MTJ.",
